{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"length","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","reasoning_content":"We have CNF with 12 variables. Clauses list. Need count of satisfying assignments. Use enumeration? 12 vars => 4096 possibilities. Could use tool enumerate? but we can compute logically. Let's analyze constraints.\n\nClauses:\n\n1. [6,2] => (x6 ∨ x2)\n2. [-5,10] => (¬x5 ∨ x10)\n3. [-4,12] => (¬x4 ∨ x12)\n4. [-9,8] => (¬x9 ∨ x8)\n5. [-1,8] => (¬x1 ∨ x8)\n6. [-11,10] => (¬x11 ∨ x10)\n7. [-7,12] => (¬x7 ∨ x12)\n8. [11,5] => (x11 ∨ x5)\n9. [4,7] => (x4 ∨ x7)\n10. [9,1] => (x9 ∨ x1)\n11. [-6,3] => (¬x6 ∨ x3)\n12. [-2,3] => (¬x2 ∨ x3)\n\nWe need count of assignments satisfying all.\n\nWe can analyze dependencies.\n\nFrom clause 1: x6 ∨ x2 must be true. So at least one of x6,x2 true.\n\nClause 11: ¬x6 ∨ x3 => if x6 true then x3 true. If x6 false then clause satisfied regardless of x3.\n\nClause 12: ¬x2 ∨ x3 => if x2 true then x3 true. If x2 false then satisfied.\n\nThus if either x6 or x2 true, then x3 must be true. Actually if both false, clause 1 violated. So at least one true, and that true forces x3 true. So x3 must be true whenever at least one of x6,x2 true. But since at least one must be true, x3 must be true always. So x3 = 1 forced.\n\nGood.\n\nNow consider clauses 2,6,8: They involve x5,x10,x11.\n\nClause 2: ¬x5 ∨ x10 => if x5 true then x10 true.\n\nClause 6: ¬x11 ∨ x10 => if x11 true then x10 true.\n\nClause 8: x11 ∨ x5 => at least one of x11,x5 true.\n\nThus we have: at least one of x5,x11 true. If either true, then x10 must be true. So x10 must be true if x5 or x11 true. But at least one is true, so x10 must be true. So x10 = 1 forced.\n\nThus x10=1, x3=1.\n\nNow clauses 3,7,9 involve x4,x7,x12.\n\nClause 3: ¬x4 ∨ x12 => if x4 true then x12 true.\n\nClause 7: ¬x7 ∨ x12 => if x7 true then x12 true.\n\nClause 9: x4 ∨ x7 => at least one of x4,x7 true.\n\nThus at least one of x4,x7 true. If either true, then x12 true. So x12 must be true. So x12=1 forced.\n\nNow clauses 4,5,10 involve x1,x8,x9.\n\nClause 4: ¬x9 ∨ x8 => if x9 true then x8 true.\n\nClause 5: ¬x1 ∨ x8 => if x1 true then x8 true"}}],"created":1790937128,"model":"C:\\Users\\d2j3\\Documents\\Codex\\2026-09-10\\napraw\\outputs\\moon-native\\models\\gpt-oss-20b-MXFP4.gguf","system_fingerprint":"b10809-5266f24da","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":768,"prompt_tokens":3798,"total_tokens":4566,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-etHbZEfHALQpppqaadtKoq8YAu0ODWvP","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":3798,"prompt_ms":489.022,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.1287577672459189,"prompt_per_second":7766.5217515776385,"predicted_n":768,"predicted_ms":2459.919,"predicted_per_token_ms":3.2071955671447197,"predicted_per_second":311.79888443481275}}